WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.653 --> 00:00:11.534
felt excited.

2
00:00:12.894 --> 00:00:15.136
They were helping Chef at the farmstand again.

3
00:00:16.256 --> 00:00:18.017
Last time the goats had caused trouble.

4
00:00:19.038 --> 00:00:20.979
She hoped things would go smoothly today.

5
00:00:20.999 --> 00:00:25.381
"We're making deviled eggs to sell," Chef said.

6
00:00:25.401 --> 00:00:28.903
"Why are they called deviled?"

7
00:00:29.283 --> 00:00:30.064
Bobby asked.

8
00:00:31.636 --> 00:00:36.119
"A long time ago some spicy foods were called deviled," Chef said.

9
00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:38.901
Izzie looked nervous.

10
00:00:38.921 --> 00:00:42.624
"Don't worry, Izzie," Chef said.

11
00:00:42.644 --> 00:00:45.306
"Our eggs won't be very spicy."

12
00:00:47.487 --> 00:00:50.229
He filled a pot with water and put some eggs inside.

13
00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:52.691
He turned on the stovetop.

14
00:00:52.711 --> 00:00:55.212
"First, we'll hard-boil the eggs."

15
00:00:56.633 --> 00:01:00.016
After the water started boiling, Chef turned off the stovetop.

16
00:01:01.076 --> 00:01:02.277
He put a lid on the pot.

17
00:01:02.297 --> 00:01:06.581
"The eggs will cook in the hot water," he said.

18
00:01:06.601 --> 00:01:08.983
"Let's get the farmstand ready."

19
00:01:12.006 --> 00:01:14.187
Chef and the kids set up tables outside.

20
00:01:16.389 --> 00:01:17.530
Nina looked at the goats.

21
00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:20.733
"You'd better be good today!"

22
00:01:20.753 --> 00:01:23.916
"I'll keep an eye on them," Jason said.

23
00:01:25.697 --> 00:01:28.340
Fifteen minutes later everyone went back inside.

24
00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:33.202
Chef drained water from the pot.

25
00:01:35.003 --> 00:01:38.366
The kids carefully plunged the hard-boiled eggs into ice water.

26
00:01:38.386 --> 00:01:44.891
"Cold water stops the eggs from cooking further," Chef said.

27
00:01:44.911 --> 00:01:47.874
"It makes them easier to peel too."

28
00:01:50.676 --> 00:01:53.759
The kids went outside to pick vegetables while the eggs cooled.

29
00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:56.521
Nina picked tomatoes.

30
00:01:58.603 --> 00:01:59.984
The goats played in their pen.

31
00:02:01.372 --> 00:02:02.693
She shook her finger at them.

32
00:02:02.713 --> 00:02:06.576
"These vegetables are for customers.

33
00:02:06.957 --> 00:02:07.858
Not you!"

34
00:02:07.878 --> 00:02:13.022
"Let's take the vegetables to the farmstand now," Bobby said.

35
00:02:13.042 --> 00:02:15.344
"Away from the goats!"

36
00:02:15.364 --> 00:02:18.366
"Yes!" Nina said.

37
00:02:20.628 --> 00:02:23.430
Back inside, Izzie removed the eggs from the water.

38
00:02:24.952 --> 00:02:27.073
Everyone dried them and peeled off their shells.

39
00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:29.916
Bobby looked at the recipe screen.

40
00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:33.121
"Now we make the filling."

41
00:02:35.022 --> 00:02:38.283
They sliced the eggs in half lengthwise and scooped out the yolks.

42
00:02:40.184 --> 00:02:42.465
In a bowl they mashed the yolks with a fork.

43
00:02:44.226 --> 00:02:45.567
Jason added mayonnaise.

44
00:02:47.227 --> 00:02:48.688
Izzie added yellow mustard.

45
00:02:50.309 --> 00:02:52.750
Nina added vinegar and salt and black pepper.

46
00:02:55.211 --> 00:02:56.872
Jason stirred everything together.

47
00:02:59.008 --> 00:03:01.810
Then they filled all the egg halves with the yolk mixture.

48
00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:05.953
"Last step," Chef said.

49
00:03:05.973 --> 00:03:08.114
"We'll prepare the garnishes."

50
00:03:09.736 --> 00:03:12.958
The kids chopped parsley and green onions, and sliced radishes.

51
00:03:14.799 --> 00:03:16.761
They put the garnishes on top of the eggs.

52
00:03:18.041 --> 00:03:19.863
Izzie sprinkled on some paprika.

53
00:03:21.304 --> 00:03:25.346
"They look so pretty!

54
00:03:26.327 --> 00:03:27.268
Can we try them?"

55
00:03:28.936 --> 00:03:30.277
"Sure," Chef said.

56
00:03:31.879 --> 00:03:34.381
After their snack they were ready for the farmstand.

57
00:03:38.624 --> 00:03:40.686
Chef and Izzie carried trays of eggs.

58
00:03:41.987 --> 00:03:43.728
Nina held onto the cashbox.

59
00:03:45.069 --> 00:03:48.352
Jason and Bobby led two baby goats for the customers to pet.

60
00:03:50.133 --> 00:03:52.235
"Keep them away from the vegetables!"

61
00:03:52.675 --> 00:03:53.356
Nina said.

62
00:03:55.077 --> 00:03:55.998
Jason sighed.

63
00:03:56.538 --> 00:03:58.140
"I will!"

64
00:04:00.844 --> 00:04:02.164
The farmstand was busy.

65
00:04:04.365 --> 00:04:06.906
Nina took money from customers and gave out change.

66
00:04:10.027 --> 00:04:12.968
When everything was sold, they walked back to the farmhouse.

67
00:04:14.608 --> 00:04:15.929
Nina led one of the goats.

68
00:04:15.949 --> 00:04:22.090
"Hooray! The goats didn't ruin the farmstand today!"

69
00:04:25.711 --> 00:04:29.804
She and Jason put them in their pen.

70
00:04:29.824 --> 00:04:30.925
"How much money did we make?"

71
00:04:31.325 --> 00:04:32.005
Chef asked.

72
00:04:33.866 --> 00:04:34.766
Nina gasped.

73
00:04:36.787 --> 00:04:37.267
"Oh, no!

74
00:04:37.887 --> 00:04:39.608
I forgot the cashbox!"

75
00:04:41.409 --> 00:04:43.570
She and Bobby ran back to the farmstand.

76
00:04:45.270 --> 00:04:46.471
Nina wanted to cry.

77
00:04:46.491 --> 00:04:50.233
"If the money is gone, it's my fault!"

78
00:04:51.793 --> 00:04:54.574
But the cashbox was still there with the money inside.

79
00:04:56.095 --> 00:04:56.935
Nina sighed.

80
00:04:59.388 --> 00:05:00.749
"The goats were fine.

81
00:05:01.970 --> 00:05:05.133
But I almost ruined the farmstand this time!"
